   "source": [
    "# NOTEBOOK 09 — JOB MATCHING\n",
    "\n",
    "## Project\n",
    "Job Market Analyzer for Career Readiness in South Africa\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Calculate individual job match scores by combining skill match, text similarity, experience match, education match, and preference alignment.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Position in Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "Previous: Notebook 08 — TF-IDF & Similarity\n",
    "\n",
    "Current: Notebook 09\n",
    "\n",
    "Next: Notebook 10 — Machine Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "## Main Objective\n",
    "Calculate a final match score for each job and identify matched/missing skills.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Input\n",
    "- `data/processed/sa_it_jobs_with_similarity.csv` — jobs with similarity scores\n",
    "- `data/processed/candidate_profile.json` — candidate profile\n",
    "\n",
    "## Output\n",
    "- Job match scores for all jobs\n",
    "- Matched and missing skills per job\n",
    "- Match explanation\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# NOTEBOOK ROADMAP\n",
    "\n",
    "STEP 1 — Define Matching Objective\n",
    "STEP 2 — Load Candidate Profile\n",
    "STEP 3 — Load Target Job\n",
    "STEP 4 — Compare Skills\n",
    "STEP 5 — Calculate Skill Match\n",
    "STEP 6 — Calculate Text Similarity\n",
    "STEP 7 — Calculate Experience Match\n",
    "STEP 8 — Calculate Education Match\n",
    "STEP 9 — Calculate Target Role Relevance\n",
    "STEP 10 — Calculate Preference Alignment\n",
    "STEP 11 — Combine Component Scores\n",
    "STEP 12 — Calculate Final Match Score\n",
    "STEP 13 — Identify Matched Skills\n",
    "STEP 14 — Identify Missing Skills\n",
    "STEP 15 — Explain the Match\n",
    "STEP 16 — Validate the Result\n",
    "STEP 17 — Interpret the Result\n",
    "STEP 18 — Save Matching Results"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 1 — Define Matching Objective\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Establish the job matching methodology.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Matching Formula\n",
    "Final Match Score = w_s × Skill Match + w_e × Education Match + w_x × Experience Match + w_p × Project Relevance + w_c × CV-Job Similarity\n",
    "\n",
    "## Weights (Design Choices)\n",
    "- Skills: 40%\n",
    "- Education: 15%\n",
    "- Experience: 15%\n",
    "- Projects: 10%\n",
    "- Semantic Similarity: 20%\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Calculate each component separately, then combine with weights."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 2 — Load Candidate Profile\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Load the candidate profile for matching.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Load the candidate profile JSON."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load candidate profile\n",
    "import json\n",
    "\n",
    "with open('data/processed/candidate_profile.json', 'r') as f:\n",
    "    candidate = json.load(f)\n",
    "\n",
    "candidate_skills = set(s.lower() for s in candidate['skills'])\n",
    "print(f\"Candidate skills: {candidate_skills}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 3 — Load Target Job\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Load the job dataset with similarity scores.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Load the processed dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load job dataset\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('data/processed/sa_it_jobs_with_similarity.csv')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Job dataset loaded: {df.shape[0]} jobs\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 4 — Compare Skills\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Compare candidate skills with job requirements.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Extract job skills and compare with candidate skills."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Extract job skills\n",
    "def extract_job_skills(skills_str):\n",
    "    if pd.isna(skills_str):\n",
    "        return set()\n",
    "    return set(s.strip().lower() for s in str(skills_str).split(','))\n",
    "\n",
    "df['job_skills'] = df['Skills'].apply(extract_job_skills)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compare skills for each job\n",
    "def compare_skills(job_skills, candidate_skills):\n",
    "    matched = job_skills & candidate_skills\n",
    "    missing = job_skills - candidate_skills\n",
    "    return matched, missing\n",
    "\n",
    "df['matched_skills'] = df['job_skills'].apply(lambda x: compare_skills(x, candidate_skills)[0])\n",
    "df['missing_skills'] = df['job_skills'].apply(lambda x: compare_skills(x, candidate_skills)[1])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Skill comparison completed for all jobs.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 5 — Calculate Skill Match\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Calculate the skill match percentage.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Formula\n",
    "Skill Match = (Number of matched skills / Number of required skills) × 100\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Calculate for each job."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate skill match\n",
    "def calculate_skill_match(row):\n",
    "    total_skills = len(row['job_skills'])\n",
    "    if total_skills == 0:\n",
    "        return 0\n",
    "    matched = len(row['matched_skills'])\n",
    "    return (matched / total_skills) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "df['skill_match'] = df.apply(calculate_skill_match, axis=1).round(2)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Skill Match Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(df['skill_match'].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 6 — Calculate Text Similarity\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Use the TF-IDF similarity score from Notebook 08.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Use the pre-calculated similarity score."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Text similarity (already calculated)\n",
    "df['text_similarity'] = df['tfidf_similarity_score']\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Text Similarity Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(df['text_similarity'].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 7 — Calculate Experience Match\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Compare candidate experience with job requirements.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Formula\n",
    "Experience Coverage = min(Candidate Experience / Required Experience, 1) × 100\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Calculate for each job."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate experience match\n",
    "candidate_experience = 0  # Entry-level candidate\n",
    "\n",
    "def calculate_experience_match(required_years):\n",
    "    if pd.isna(required_years) or required_years == 0:\n",
    "        return 100  # No experience required\n",
    "    return min(candidate_experience / required_years, 1) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "df['experience_match'] = df['Experience_Years'].apply(calculate_experience_match).round(2)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Experience Match Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(df['experience_match'].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 8 — Calculate Education Match\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Compare candidate education with job requirements.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Use education level encoding to calculate match."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate education match\n",
    "candidate_education_level = 5  # Bachelor's degree\n",
    "\n",
    "def calculate_education_match(required_level):\n",
    "    if pd.isna(required_level):\n",
    "        return 100  # Not specified\n",
    "    if candidate_education_level >= required_level:\n",
    "        return 100\n",
    "    return (candidate_education_level / required_level) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "df['education_match'] = df['education_level'].apply(calculate_education_match).round(2)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Education Match Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(df['education_match'].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 9 — Calculate Target Role Relevance\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose",
    "Determine how relevant the job is to the candidate's target role.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Use keyword matching between job title and target role."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate target role relevance\n",
    "target_role = \"data analyst\"  # Candidate's target role\n",
    "\n",
    "def calculate_role_relevance(job_title):\n",
    "    if pd.isna(job_title):\n",
    "        return 0\n",
    "    job_title_lower = str(job_title).lower()\n",
    "    if target_role in job_title_lower:\n",
    "        return 100\n",
    "    # Check for related terms\n",
    "    related_terms = ['data', 'analyst', 'analytics', 'bi', 'business intelligence']\n",
    "    matches = sum(1 for term in related_terms if term in job_title_lower)\n",
    "    return min(matches * 20, 80)\n",
    "\n",
    "df['role_relevance'] = df['Job_Title_Normalized'].apply(calculate_role_relevance).round(2)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Role Relevance Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(df['role_relevance'].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 10 — Calculate Preference Alignment\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose",
    "Check if the job matches candidate preferences.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Compare job characteristics with candidate preferences."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate preference alignment\n",
    "candidate_preferences = {\n",
    "    'preferred_location': 'gauteng',\n",
    "    'preferred_work_type': 'hybrid',\n    "    'preferred_employment_type': 'full-time'\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "def calculate_preference_alignment(row):\n",
    "    score = 0\n",
    "    checks = 0\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Location preference\n",
    "    if candidate_preferences['preferred_location']:\n",
    "        checks += 1\n",
    "        if candidate_preferences['preferred_location'] in str(row['Province']).lower():\n",
    "            score += 1\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Work type preference\n",
    "    if candidate_preferences['preferred_work_type']:\n",
    "        checks += 1\n",
    "        if candidate_preferences['preferred_work_type'] in str(row['Remote']).lower():\n",
    "            score += 1\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Employment type preference\n",
    "    if candidate_preferences['preferred_employment_type']:\n",
    "        checks += 1\n",
    "        if candidate_preferences['preferred_employment_type'] in str(row['Employment_Type']).lower():\n",
    "            score += 1\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return (score / checks * 100) if checks > 0 else 50\n",
    "\n",
    "df['preference_alignment'] = df.apply(calculate_preference_alignment, axis=1).round(2)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Preference Alignment Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(df['preference_alignment'].describe())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# STEP 11 — Combine Component Scores\n",
    "\n",
    "## Purpose\n",
    "Combine all component scores with weights.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Weights (Design Choices)\n",
    "- Skills: 40%\n",
    "- Education: 15%\n",
    "- Experience: 15%\n",
    "- Projects: 10%\n",
    "- Semantic Similarity: 20%\n",
    "\n",
    "## Method\n",
    "Calculate weighted sum of all components."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Combine component scores\n",
    "weights = {\n",
    "    'skill_match': 0.40,\n",
    "    'education_match': 0.15,\n",
    "    'experience_match': 0.15,\n",
    "    'role_relevance': 0.10,\n",
    "    'text_similarity': 0.20\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "df['match_score'] = (\n",
    "    df['skill_match'] * weights['skill_match'] +\n",
    "    df['education_match'] * weights['education_match'] +\n",
    "    df['experience_match'] * weights['experience_match'] +\n",
    "    df['role_relevance'] * weights['role_relevance'] +\n",
    "    df['text_similarity'] * weights['text_similarity']\n",
    ").round(2)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Match Score Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(df['match_score'].describe())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTop 10 Matching Jobs:\")\n",
    "top_10 = df.nlargest(10, 'match_score')[['Job_Title', 'Company', 'Province', 'match_score', 'skill_match', 'text_similarity']]\n",
    "print(top_10.to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
